const report=`# l8: photo detail on the published 3D skeleton\n\nThe photo now supplies the on-sky detail. Distance, disc plane, warp and bar placement remain fixed to the accepted research model. The 512-pixel sheet includes Earth versus Horálek, face-on, 45 degrees, edge-on and a face-on comparison with NGC 4027.\n\n![l8 sheet](sheet.png)\n\n## Conversion\n\nThe preserved NOX diffuse image supplies the cleaned input. [Original versus cleaned](cleaning.png) shows compact light removed while extended nebulae remain. This is compact-source suppression, not a foreground-membership catalogue; compact LMC sources may also have been removed. The original is retained unchanged.\n\nA fixed BC03 color basis represents old and hot young stars. Hydrogen recombination lines through the preserved Johnson filters seed the gas color. One global pink-gas tint accounts for unknown photo passbands, processing and missing metal lines before the spectral inverse. There are no fitted pixel or regional templates.\n\nDust is a fixed dark-lane and reddening proxy under the Gordon LMC law. Bell fixes one global column budget, with mean line-of-sight V optical depth ${num(bell.meanObservedLosTauV).toFixed(4)}. Its spatial holes are not copied. The fields are de-tilted through the plane and warp, then distributed vertically with separate Gaussian profiles. An observer-ray extrusion was rejected because it made streaks.\n\nThe photo boundary blends over 20 source pixels into the paper Gaussian stellar disc and its recorded faint outskirts. The normalization uses all boundary samples, including zeros. Young light, gas and dust beyond the photo remain unsupported. [The 40-kpc surroundings](surroundings-40kpc-100x.png) use an explicitly marked 100-fold diagnostic exposure; the continuation is stellar, not a gas envelope.\n\n## Depth widths\n\n| Component | Gaussian sigma | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Old disc | 410 pc | Kacharov published model |\n| Bar | 241 pc | Conditional adopted vertical ratio |\n| Young stars | 100 pc | Thin-layer assumption |\n| Gas | 100 pc | Thin-layer assumption |\n| Dust | 205 pc | Intermediate-layer assumption |\n\nThe accepted research does not supply precise measured heights for every component. These assumptions are exposed rather than described as measurements.\n\n## Source round-trip\n\n| Residual at 512 pixels | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n${roundtrip}\n\nBoth checkerboards supplied source pixels to the deterministic conversion. Their residuals test reprojection and global grading; they are not independent validation of the inferred depth. Finite thickness blurs Earth's view, and the faint outer annulus remains too bright.\n\nChannel-share errors, in red, green and blue percentage points:\n\n${array(stats.channelShareDifferencePercentagePoints).map((v,i)=>`- ${['Inner 1.5 kpc','1.5–4 kpc','Outer region'][i]}: ${numbers(v).map(x=>x.toFixed(2)).join(', ')}.`).join('\n')}\n\n## Survey checks\n\n| Dataset | Samples | Check value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n${checkTable}\n\nValues are Pearson correlations except Bell mean, which is inferred divided by measured column. [The check definitions and limitations](checks.md) distinguish calibration from validation. Strong blue-count and H-alpha agreement supports those classifications. VMC ages and local dust remain weaker checks; they were not fitted away. WISE brightness also depends on temperature and illumination.\n\n## Limits and verification\n\nThe 45-degree view retains some vertical elongation and a photo-footprint imprint. This candidate is not qualified for baking.\n\nRGB cannot uniquely separate stellar ages, metal lines and extinction. ${(100*num(split.fractionOutsidePositiveCone)).toFixed(1)}% of valid pixels fall outside the positive fixed-color cone; prescribed clipping preserves total RGB light. The brightness-weighted color reconstruction RMS before global grading is ${(100*num(split.relativeRgbReconstructionRms)).toFixed(2)}%. [The component maps](components.png) make the partition inspectable. No individual nebular depths are measured.\n\n| Rung | Render width | Total rung time |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n${runTime}\n\nTwenty-eight behavior tests and strict TypeScript pass. Seven deletion checks catch removal of the spectral conversion, global gas grade, photo renderer, vertical-depth rule, distinct heights, Bell normalization and exterior profile. All requested final views were inspected. Only the authorized tiny and 512-pixel small rungs ran. No GPU training, native-resolution multi-start fit, slab bake, shared-package change, commit or publication occurred.\n\nPhoto credit: NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/P. Horálek (Institute of Physics in Opava), [source](https://noirlab.edu/public/images/iotw2547a/), CC BY 4.0. External comparison: ESO, [NGC 4027](https://www.eso.org/public/images/potw1030a/).\n`;
